WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.262
These are the main habits from Module 9.

00:00:02.262 --> 00:00:07.122
Profile before cleaning. Preserve uncertainty rather than inventing corrections.

00:00:07.122 --> 00:00:12.067
Keep standardization, validation, duplicate handling, and correction conceptually separate.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:17.987
Use views, quarantine patterns, transactions, and lineage to make work safer and reproducible.

00:00:17.987 --> 00:00:20.652
Add constraints after the rules are stable.

00:00:20.652 --> 00:00:25.222
And keep quality dimensions visible instead of hiding everything behind one score.

00:00:25.222 --> 00:00:30.332
Connect this idea to a customer master-data project cleaning duplicate profiles.

00:00:30.332 --> 00:00:35.087
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:35.087 --> 00:00:41.617
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:41.617 --> 00:00:46.662
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:46.662 --> 00:00:51.599
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
